        "index": 125,
        "field": "context",
        "old": "\u2026r both \ud835\udc4b and \ud835\udc43 , and moreover for powers of them. Defining the uncertainty for an observable by a standard deviation, we have \ud835\udf0e \ud835\udc4b = \u27e8 \ud835\udc4b 2 \u27e9 \u2212 \u27e8 \ud835\udc4b \u27e9 2 , and likewise for the momentum: \ud835\udf0e \ud835\udc43 = \u27e8 \ud835\udc43 2 \u27e9 \u2212 \u27e8 \ud835\udc43 \u27e9 2 . The uncertainty principle states that \ud835\u2026",
        "new": "\u2026r both \ud835\udc4b and \ud835\udc43 , and moreover for powers of them. Defining the uncertainty for an observable by a standard deviation, we have \ud835\udf0e \ud835\udc4b = \u27e8 \ud835\udc4b 2 \u27e9 \u2212 \u27e8 \ud835\udc4b \u27e9 2 , and likewise for the momentum: \ud835\udf0e \ud835\udc43 = \u27e8 \ud835\udc43 2 \u27e9 \u2212 \u27e8 \ud835\udc43 \u27e9 2 . The uncertainty principle states that \u2026"
      },
      {
        "index": 126,
        "field": "context",
